<title>HONG KONG: Tai Cheung interim profit surges 59 pct.</title>
<headline>Tai Cheung interim profit surges 59 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   13.0  vs 8.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0   vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  6.6   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    78.8  vs 49.5</p>
<p>    Turnover		     114.7 vs 83.2</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tai Cheung Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 13-17</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   February 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Tai Cheung Holdings is a property group.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$6.6 million on sales of shares of the company's 10 percent owned Lee Gardens International Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
